<dashboard version="1.1" script="s2f_setup.js">
    <label>Configuration</label>
    <description>Configure CrowdStrike Falcon tenants, API credentials, the default Fusion workflow, Next-Gen SIEM HEC, and corporate proxy settings.</description>

    <row>
        <panel>
            <html>
                <div style="max-width: 760px; padding: 12px;">
                    <div id="s2f_status_banner" style="display:none; padding: 10px 14px; margin-bottom: 16px; border-radius: 4px; font-weight: 600;"></div>

                    <p style="margin-top: 0; color: #444;">
                        This page controls how notable events reach CrowdStrike. Each tenant keeps its own
                        credentials and settings. Secrets are stored encrypted in Splunk and are never written to the
                        configuration file.
                    </p>

                    <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">Tenant</h3>
                    <div style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
                        <label style="display:block; font-weight:600;">CrowdStrike Tenant (CID)</label>
                        <select id="s2f_cid_name" style="width: 100%; max-width: 420px;"></select>
                        <div style="font-size:12px; color:#666; margin-top:4px;">
                            Pick an existing tenant, or <strong>+ New tenant...</strong> to add one. The name
                            matches the alert action's <code>cid</code> parameter; <code>default</code> is the primary
                            tenant.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <h3>1. CrowdStrike Falcon OAuth2 &amp; Fusion SOAR</h3>
                    <div style="margin-bottom: 10px;">
                        <label style="display:block; font-weight:600;">Falcon Cloud Region</label>
                        <select data-field="falcon_cloud" style="width: 100%; max-width: 420px;">
                            <option value="eu-1">eu-1 (https://api.eu-1.crowdstrike.com)</option>
                            <option value="us-1">us-1 (https://api.crowdstrike.com)</option>
                            <option value="us-2">us-2 (https://api.us-2.crowdstrike.com)</option>
                            <option value="us-gov-1">us-gov-1 (https://api.laggar.gcw.crowdstrike.com)</option>
                            <option value="us-gov-2">us-gov-2 (https://api.us-gov-2.crowdstrike.mil)</option>
                        </select>
                        <div style="font-size:12px; color:#666; margin-top:4px;">
                            The Falcon API region for this tenant. Choose the region shown in your Falcon console URL.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div style="margin-bottom: 10px;">
                        <label style="display:block; font-weight:600;">OAuth2 API Client ID</label>
                        <input type="text" data-field="client_id" placeholder="32-character Client ID" style="width: 100%; max-width: 420px;" />
                        <div style="font-size:12px; color:#666; margin-top:4px;">
                            Create the client in Falcon Console under <strong>Support and resources &gt; API clients and keys</strong>.
                            Grant <strong>Workflows: Write</strong> and <strong>Next-Gen SIEM: Write</strong>; add the
                            Cases and IOC scopes when the alert actions use them.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div style="margin-bottom: 10px;">
                        <label style="display:block; font-weight:600;">OAuth2 API Client Secret <span id="s2f_secret_badge" style="font-weight:normal; font-size:12px; color:#53a051;"></span></label>
                        <input type="password" data-field="client_secret" placeholder="Leave blank to keep existing stored secret" autocomplete="new-password" style="width: 100%; max-width: 420px;" />
                        <div style="font-size:12px; color:#666; margin-top:4px;">
                            Stored encrypted in Splunk's credential store. Leave blank to keep the existing secret.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
                        <label style="display:block; font-weight:600;">Default Fusion Workflow (Definition ID or Name)</label>
                        <input type="text" data-field="default_workflow" placeholder="e.g. 32-char definition_id or workflow name" style="width: 100%; max-width: 420px;" />
                        <div style="font-size:12px; color:#666; margin-top:4px;">
                            The workflow used when the alert action does not override it. Use the 32-character
                            definition ID (recommended) or the workflow name.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <h3>2. Next-Gen SIEM HEC (Optional)</h3>
                    <div style="margin-bottom: 10px;">
                        <label style="display:block; font-weight:600;">NG-SIEM HEC Collector URL</label>
                        <input type="text" data-field="ngsiem_hec_url" placeholder="https://.../services/collector" style="width: 100%; max-width: 520px;" />
                        <div style="font-size:12px; color:#666; margin-top:4px;">
                            Required only for <code>ngsiem_hec</code> or <code>both</code>. Use the full collector URL
                            from Falcon Next-Gen SIEM.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
                        <label style="display:block; font-weight:600;">NG-SIEM HEC Token <span id="s2f_hec_badge" style="font-weight:normal; font-size:12px; color:#53a051;"></span></label>
                        <input type="password" data-field="hec_token" placeholder="Leave blank to keep existing stored token" autocomplete="new-password" style="width: 100%; max-width: 420px;" />
                        <div style="font-size:12px; color:#666; margin-top:4px;">
                            Stored encrypted per tenant. Leave blank to keep the existing token.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <h3>3. Advanced</h3>
                    <details style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
                        <summary style="cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600;">Proxy &amp; custom CA</summary>
                        <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
                            <label style="display:block; font-weight:600;">HTTP/HTTPS Proxy URL</label>
                            <input type="text" data-field="proxy_url" placeholder="http://proxy.example.com:8080" style="width: 100%; max-width: 420px;" />
                            <div style="font-size:12px; color:#666; margin-top:4px;">
                                Optional. Include credentials in the URL if the proxy requires them.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
                            <label style="display:block; font-weight:600;">Custom CA Bundle Path (Optional)</label>
                            <input type="text" data-field="ca_bundle_path" placeholder="/opt/splunk/etc/apps/TA-splunk_to_fusion/certs/corp_ca.pem" style="width: 100%; max-width: 520px;" />
                            <div style="font-size:12px; color:#666; margin-top:4px;">
                                Optional. Leave empty to load every <code>.pem</code> and <code>.crt</code> file from the
                                app's <code>certs/</code> directory.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </details>

                    <div style="margin-top: 18px;">
                        <button type="button" id="s2f_btn_save" class="btn btn-primary" style="margin-right: 10px;">Save Configuration</button>
                        <button type="button" id="s2f_btn_test" class="btn">Test CrowdStrike Connection</button>
                    </div>

                    <p style="margin-top: 16px; font-size: 12px; color: #666;">
                        Case creation and IOC saving are configured per alert action, not on this page. Open the
                        alert action's settings on a detection rule to set them.
                    </p>

                    <p style="margin-top: 16px; font-size: 12px; color: #666;">
                        Only users with the <code>s2f_admin</code> capability (or <code>admin_all_objects</code>) can
                        save configuration. Analysts with <code>s2f_send</code> can run the alert action but cannot
                        change these settings.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </html>
        </panel>
    </row>
</dashboard>
